            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Echocardiographic assessment of changes in wall motion and ventricular dimensions with exercise may be of significant value in the evaluation of the patient with coronary artery disease. Topics covered in this article include exercise physiology, dynamic M-mode echocardiography and its limitations, two-dimensional dynamic exercise echocardiography, and echocardiography during isometric exercise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
